---
description: Design handoff rules for the Design Studio Calendar page (KIS Creativity Space)
alwaysApply: false
---

When implementing the Design Studio Calendar page:

- The spec is handoff_cursor_studio_calendar/README.md — cell precedence, colors, tags, and copy are exact.
- designs/*.dc.html are HTML prototypes for behavior reference only. Never copy their markup, the DCLogic classes, or support.js.
- The page is strictly read-only: no click handlers, no hover affordances, no auth gate. It's a projection of existing data, not a new store.
- Cell precedence: space booking → training session → block → free/no-school. Blocks of EVERY scope render, honoring the weekly [start, until] range, each in its own color family: training-only = amber stripes (#fdf4e3/#f7e7c3/#eeddb2, tag CLASSES OK · NO TRAINING), space-only = blue stripes (#e6edf4/#d3e0ec/#b9cede, tag TRAINING OK · NO CLASSES), all = red stripes (#fbeeee/#f3dcdc/#eccfcf, tag FULLY CLOSED). Never collapse them into one color.
- Reuse the booking pages' grid skeleton, day-color chips (school-calendar json), week-arrow behavior (current + 2), and legend styling — this page must feel like a sibling of those two.
- Update live when bookings/sessions/blocks change.
